  "body": "This is a follow-up to https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/179983e9eb99efe417349a40ebb664bd11668ddd. See [related discussion on #whatwg IRC](http://logs.glob.uno/?c=freenode%23whatwg&s=4%20Mar%202016&e=4%20Mar%202016#c987799).\n\nIn the end I left out making any changes to the [Other link types](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#other-link-types) section as part of this, the reason being that most people/specs will never need to create and register a `body-ok` keyword, so we don’t need to burden them all with it in that section (which is primarly just registration instructions). \n\nProbably only other spec editors should actually be adding any `body-ok` keywords, and if/when they do, they should rightly be coordinating it with us and the rest of the community before doing it unilaterally.\n\nAnd that’s a very different case than the typical `rel` keywords registered by individual that usually don’t actually affect UA behavior (and so we don’t have to know much about nor care much about)—which is what the main intended audience of the  [Other link types](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#other-link-types) section section is. And so which is why I think we don’t need to any info about `body-ok` to that section.\n",
